.TH "GLESHA-RETRY" "1" "" "glesha" "User Commands"
.nh
.ad l
.SH NAME
glesha\-retry \- resume the pending operation of a set
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBglesha retry\fR SET [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Resume the interrupted operation of SET. Completed archives and finished uploads are reused. If nothing is pending but registry copies are out of date, they are repaired.
.PP
Use \-\-archive FILE if the completed archive of a pending run was moved.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-archive FILE
Use the completed archive moved to FILE.
.SS Remote options
.TP
.B \-\-to REMOTE...
Limit bucket access to REMOTE.
.TP
.B \-\-from REMOTE...
Limit bucket access to REMOTE.
.PP
REMOTE... takes a comma\-separated list and may be repeated. If \-\-from or \-\-to is given, no other remote is accessed.
.SS Archive options
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-archive
Keep the local archive after a successful upload.
.SS Passphrase options
.TP
.B \-\-catalog\-passphrase\-file FILE
Read the catalog passphrase from FILE ('\-': stdin). Without this option, GLESHA_CATALOG_PASSPHRASE or a hidden prompt is used.
.PP
The global options described in glesha(1) are also accepted.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
glesha retry docs
glesha retry docs \-\-archive /mnt/spare/docs.tar.xz.gpg
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glesha (1),
.BR glesha\-catalog (1),
.BR glesha\-run (1)
